            <span class="eyebrow">Digital book</span>
            <h1>A guide to prayer and reflection for your everyday life</h1>
            <p class="lede">
                Seven chapters with Bible passages, brief reflections, and space
                to write. Designed for anyone who wants to build a consistent
                prayer practice, with short readings that fit into a daily routine.
            </p>
            <div class="cta-wrap">
                <a class="cta" href="#oferta">See what's included and the price</a>
                <p class="cta-note">Instant digital access · 7-day guarantee</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ABOUT THE MATERIAL -->
    <section>
        <div class="wrap">
            <h2>What this material is</h2>
            <p class="sub">A digital book, not a course or a consulting service.</p>
            <p>
                <strong>The Ancient Manuscript</strong> is a written guide
                that brings together Bible passages, brief reflections, and prayers
                organized by theme. Each chapter offers a short reading,
                a question to reflect on, and blank space to write down
                whatever you would like to record.
            </p>
            <p>
                It does not promise results or replace professional guidance.
                It is reading material for personal devotion, to use at your
                own pace: one chapter a day, one a week, or in any order you prefer.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONTENTS -->
    <section>
        <div class="wrap">
            <h2>What you'll find inside</h2>
            <p class="sub">The guide's seven chapters.</p>
            <ol class="chapters">
                <li><b>The origins of the texts</b><span>Historical context for the passages in the book and why they were brought together in this way.</span></li>
                <li><b>Making time for prayer</b><span>How to set aside a few minutes each day and create a routine you can maintain over time.</span></li>
                <li><b>Prayers of gratitude</b><span>Readings and prayers to begin the day, with space to write down what you are grateful for.</span></li>
                <li><b>Through difficult times</b><span>Passages to accompany you through seasons of doubt, loss, or weariness.</span></li>
                <li><b>Family and relationships</b><span>Reflections on close relationships and prayers for others.</span></li>
                <li><b>Consistency and patience</b><span>On maintaining your practice when you do not see immediate change.</span></li>
                <li><b>A record of your journey</b><span>Guided pages to write on and revisit later to reflect on your notes.</span></li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

